---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HeroFractal from '../components/HeroFractal.astro';

// Newest first. A text about revision should be visibly revisable.
const iterations = [
  {
    date: '2026-09-16',
    title: 'The Eighth Iteration',
    notes: [
      'A new Weave joins the Skein tier — The Only Road — bringing the catalogue to eleven Weaves and forty-nine drawable figures.',
      'Part Seven gains its matching Gathering, for eleven in all.',
      'The Loom\'s concept index adds "Solving for the third leg": your Current, theirs, and the Meeting you make are three locked elements, so knowing two gives you the third.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-09-15',
    title: 'The Seventh Iteration',
    notes: [
      'The Standing Thirds gallery now holds the whole catalogue — forty-eight drawable figures plus the Infinite Boundary, up from sixteen. Every figure is generated directly from Part Five\'s tables, so the roster can no longer drift from the book.',
      'Each figure names what it is made of. A Meeting links to the two Currents that fuse into it; a Weave links to its two Meetings — so the fusion lineage is now the navigation, in both directions.',
      'Every figure carries its Turning from Part Seven, and its card reading from the Deck.',
      'The Weaving draws from the full deck, and the laid-out reading now asks the second question: at what speed am I looking at this — Weather, Climate, or Terrain?',
      'Dyren returns to the catalogue as a seventh Long Form. Sethra is retired.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-09-15',
    title: 'The Sixth Iteration',
    notes: [
      'Part Five is rebuilt as a generative catalogue: forty-eight figures across five scales, where twelve Self-scale Currents fuse into nineteen Dyad Meetings, which fuse into ten Skein Weaves, then six Culture Long Forms, then the Infinite Boundary. A figure\'s scale is now what it is made of, not a category assigned to it.',
      'Part Seven — The Turnings is new: a calendar of shared, recurring occasions aimed at a Global Form that hasn\'t finished arriving. Twelve monthly Self turnings, nineteen undated Dyad ones, ten Skein gatherings, six Great Days fixed to solstice and equinox, and one triggered by a great comet.',
      'Weavings gains "Weather, Climate, Terrain" — every card now gets a second question after its ring: at what speed am I looking at this?',
      'The Standing Thirds gallery and the Weaving deck still run on the sixteen original figures. The catalogue they illustrate is now much larger; reconciling the two is the next piece of work.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-09-13',
    title: 'The Fifth Iteration',
    notes: [
      'The flower\'s electric field joins the Third Thing and the Fold as a literal, measurable example — a relational field altered by every visitor and read by the next as real information neither party holds alone.',
      'A precise distinction between structural realism (real independent of anyone perceiving it) and experiential realism (a feeling is real the instant it occurs, whether or not its content is true) runs through The Third Thing and Naming and Defusing.',
      'Finding Your Leverage Point and Systems Theory Foundations both grow substantially: constraint-counting for tangled decisions, the exact arithmetic behind reinforcing vs. balancing loop signs, and leverage redefined precisely as a maximally shared connection in a system\'s web of dependencies.',
      'Closing the Loop\'s three-paragraph meditation on suffering and hope is compressed to one — the same claim, said once instead of three times.',
      'The Trust Triangle, The Sacrifice Trap, and Aestren each gain a new worked example or mechanism (interpersonal complementarity, sign-flipping growth, the Fermi paradox).',
      'The Loom\'s concept index gains eight more entries reflecting all of the above.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-09-10',
    title: 'The Fourth Iteration',
    notes: [
      'The Third Thing gains the symphysical: what physical things make once their parts interact, standing beside "metaphysical" rather than above it — with emergence\'s threshold (the wetness example) and its most physically stubborn case, solidity, worked through directly.',
      'Emergence is distinguished from luck: chance is a fact about one instant, emergence a fact about the shape many instants make together — "luck = preparation + time" is corrected to a probabilistic claim about compounding exposure, not a guarantee.',
      'The Woven Self closes with the actual argument for practicing at all: the capacity to catch a reflex and choose differently is real but rare, and everything from there forward is that same capacity at a different scale each time.',
      'The Loom\'s concept index gains nine new entries — coasting vs. accelerating, open vs. closed boundaries, atomic composition and the Woven Self, resonance, the association machine, and loop period among them.',
      'Star Wars and A Short History of Nearly Everything join the Source Library.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-09-06',
    title: 'The Third Iteration',
    notes: [
      'Part One gains two chapters: Complicated or Complex, and Position, Speed, Acceleration — a working diagnostic (does anything feed back? which order am I looking at?) threaded forward into the leverage ladder, the Sacrifice Trap, and Systems Theory Foundations.',
      'Part Four is renamed The Ground Underneath.',
      'The Loop Tongue\'s vocabulary is cut from twelve words to nine — Field, Attractor, and Vector are retired. "A word that can be replaced by a plain phrase without loss should be."',
      'The old Glossary, the Spiral Index, and the Loom are merged into one appendix: The Loom — The Complete Reference. Notation, the nine words, the scale grid, and a compact index to every named concept in the book, in one place.',
      'A new named pattern, the Braid — a Skein and a Banner fused, real substance carrying a visible name — threads through Naming and Defusing, the Dyad, the Skein, and Charten.',
      'Every Part now opens stating plainly what it\'s for, what you\'ll be able to do after it, and where to go if you only want the practice.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-08-23',
    title: 'The Second Iteration',
    notes: [
      'Genesis, Fifth Iteration (Life): life now defined as running a reinforcing and a balancing loop simultaneously, not in alternation.',
      'Reading Your Own Cycle gains tides as the grounding image for why both loop types run together — the chapter’s explicit homeostasis payoff.',
      'Rethen’s epigraph changed to “Symmetry is easy balance, but balance is not always easy” — new passage on earned balance vs. cost-free symmetry.',
      'Going to Ground now names conservation of mass directly as the physical grounding for “the material returns to circulation.” Becoming a Third gains a closing echo of the same eternal cycle.',
      'A Word on Belief Itself and Closing the Loop both add explicit genre framing: this is neither self-help nor a pitch for building an organization — a rising tide, not a ledger.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: '2026-08-23',
    title: 'The First Iteration',
    notes: [
      'Site seeded from the complete handbook — all six parts, the appendix, and the full Standing Thirds roster.',
      'The chaos game runs live on the home page.',
      'Every chapter is a node with curated relations — the “follow your thread” paths.',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Iterations" description="Every revision of this living document, recorded in the open.">
  <HeroFractal type="spirals" seed="iterations" color="var(--c-p3)" />
  <h1>Iterations</h1>
  <p style="color: var(--muted);">
    This is a living document — <em>and the output of each telling becomes the input for every
    telling since, including this one.</em> Every meaningful change is recorded here.
  </p>

  {iterations.map((it) => (
    <section style="margin-top: 2.5rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--line); padding-left: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow">{it.date}</p>
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0.2em;">{it.title}</h2>
      <ul>
        {it.notes.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>
  ))}
</Base>
